  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Nightfall Shelf is the subterranean penguin colony carved into the Berg's volcanic interior, counterpart and co-dependent to the surface settlement of Aurora Stack. The Shelf's tunnel network extends from natural cavern ice through hand-carved passages into depths that predate any penguin civilization. Its economy rests on fire-core extraction — solidified volcanic heat mined from increasingly unstable geothermal veins — which the Shelf trades to the surface for aurora-crystals it cannot produce. This exchange, formalized under the Flipper Accord, keeps both colonies alive and neither satisfied.
    
    The tunnels branch in a logic that resists systematic mapping. Bioluminescent glyphs mark intersections in script that creation scripture identifies as the Berg's original writing, older than any surface text, reportedly bleeding from ice that remembers the passage of Shadow-Broker Nyla, the divine figure of Nightshelf theology. The oldest surviving examples encode operational commandments: which passages stay open, fire-core burn durations, alcove shelter capacities. Walls display their age in striations — natural ice, then tool-marked sections, then repair patches using salvaged aurora-crystal reinforcements, ceremonial bone-work, and stretches deliberately darkened by smoke to conceal what lies beneath.
    
    The deeper one descends, the colder it becomes despite the volcanic warmth — a phenomenon that defies conventional thermodynamics. The ice pulls heat downward, apparently remembering something from the Berg's primordial age. The oldest tunnels possess a visual texture that resists direct observation.
    
    ## Governance and Law
    
    **The Shadow Parliament**, a council of eleven guild-masters, holds formal authority over defense and resource allocation. The Parliament convenes in a repurposed aquifer chamber whose acoustics make plain speech inadvisable — stone seats arranged in a half-circle around a fire-core whose remaining life the guild-masters judge by feel. The Parliament has not convened in full quorum for at least two cycles, a lapse publicly attributed to restructuring. At an earlier period the council held thirteen seats; two were vacated following a purge after the Veil Vents incident, which the Nightshelf officially denies occurred.
    
    **Foedus∴silenti** governs daily conduct — a law replacing speech with smoke-oaths and fire-binding, adopted after orca raiders learned to track penguins by work-songs carried through ice-thin walls. The silence is not merely custom but survival infrastructure.
    
    **Foedus∴vincu**, originally a Faction Wars-era charter granting exclusive fire-core trading rights, has been rewritten after each major conflict until it now commemorates five wars and functions as the Shelf's de facto constitution. Its formal measure was also invoked for the diplomatic compact granting orca passage through the deep tunnels — a use that remains contested.
    
    ## The Fire Keepers
    
    The Fire Keepers tend the volcanic cores that heat the colony. Senior keepers stabilize braziers with pressure-chants and bone-work passed through generations, counting heartbeats between core-pulses with the precision surface mystics reserve for stellar parallaxes. Their negligence means freezing deaths in the outer tunnels; this is understood by all parties as fact, not rhetoric.
    
    The fire-keeper creation tradition holds that the tunnels follow paths carved by divine blood before any shaper touched stone, and that fire-cores are clots of that blood too dense to freeze. The Shelf itself is understood as a living organ that has forgotten its function but not its warmth. Fire-keepers, in this framework, are not miners but custodians of a body that has not finished dying.
    
    **Chill-breaker Sanctervilevia~ Ice**, first of the fire-keeper lineage, is recorded in smoke-oaths as *she-who-entered-the-still-beating-chamber* — the one who felt the god's heart pulse through the wall and understood that the shapers' work was containment, not carving: sealing chambers against the body's own spasms.
    
    Following the Shadow Parliament's dissolution of the Midnight Claws under the judicial decree Iudicium∴culum, the Fire Keepers inherited guard authority over the Glow-Fissure and deep-tunnel posts. They were not trained for deep-tunnel operations. The resulting command incoherence remains unresolved.
    
    ## The Midnight Claws
    
    The Midnight Claws, the syndicate that controlled the Shelf's shadow economy, moved through the same passages as the Fire Keepers with a different rhythm — handling enforcement, smuggling, and disappearances the official guilds declined to acknowledge. Their routes were marked by graffiti in a cipher most residents pretended not to understand. The Claws exploited the deep-forge access points' sealing capability to isolate targets, and were for decades the only authority the deep passages recognized.
    
    Shadow-Broker Nyla's public confession to the Aurora Stack council ended her leadership and exposed thirty winters of crimes. The Shadow Parliament dissolved the organization under Iudicium∴culum, sentencing surviving members to supervised labor-service above the third descent level. After the dissolution, the Claws' territorial control fragmented; during the Faction Wars, the ☽'ofund' Guild, a Nightshelf trade guild, conducted a supply interdiction against remaining Claw elements under Pactum∴ne emergency provisions. No formal denial-of-trade was registered with the Parliament. The records are incomplete.
    
    ## Culture and Record-Keeping
    
    The Shelf's inhabitants wear charcoal wraps embroidered with ember-thread that glows only in absolute darkness — a distinction that carries more social weight than outsiders recognize. Fledglings, called *tunnel-chicks*, stamp nursery rhymes into dark passages between markets and sleeping-nooks: counting games, dares, and lullabies whose words change by tunnel but whose rhythms hold fixed across the colony. The tunnel-mothers neither explain nor forbid them. Assessor Yunchouheixei's Cycle 847 collection documents an anomaly in these counting songs — a rhyme that invariably reaches eighteen despite mathematical inconsistency, provoking visible concern among adults who will not discuss it.
    
    Separate from the ice-memory archive that other colonies depend upon, the Shelf maintains **shadow-ledgers** — founding-era records and courier manifests kept in ink on hide. This independent archive reflects a deep institutional distrust of the aurora's frozen record-keeping. As a practice it is methodologically superior for certain categories of evidence, though I recognize I am not an impartial judge on questions of archival methodology.
    
    ## Physical Infrastructure
    
    ### Key Locations
    
    | Location | Function | Status |
    |---|---|---|
    | **Eastern ventilation shaft** | Primary tunnel-runner route for fire-core/aurora-crystal exchange | Partially collapsed; audit attributed damage to external probing, not structural failure |
    | **Glow-Fissure** | Bedrock fissure three levels below the Parliament chamber | Active corruption source; guard authority transferred to Fire Keepers after Claws' dissolution |
    | **Echo∴eliquiae** | Memorial alcove accumulating relics of fallen defenders | Active |
    | **Memoria∴moria** | Multi-level memorial complex staffed by Remembrancers | Active; fire-core lamps rationed, returned by morning |
    | **Dead-forge corridors** | Former smelting operations destroyed by the Profun∴lapsum | Sealed; walls slicked with residual fat; ongoing deep-vein collapse |
    | **Drowned Ledge** | Sealed outpost, closed three generations ago | Fire-core braziers still burn through frozen windows; thirty-seven names on the memorial wall |
    | **Western shelf** | Former tunnel network connecting western approaches to eastern depots | Collapsed during the Orca Incursion; supply lines permanently severed |
    
    **Star∴eternal**, a bone-sutured perimeter technology, reads pressure, blood, and movement through the ice to detect approaches to the deep tunnels. Below the mapped passages, courier-marks scratched in ink visible only in peripheral darkness guide navigation for those trained not to look directly.
    
    The Glow-Fissure produces a cold-hum felt through stone that rises into the teeth of anyone above it. Tunnel-chants attribute its opening to Nyla's compensatory burning to maintain the ancient seals, which cracked the first breach-point. A Shadow-Walk reconnaissance following the Claws' dissolution found the Wake-Singers, an orca cult, had breached through the Fissure's base into unmapped passages. Something non-human returned from those depths communicating in hunt-song frequencies.
    
    ## External Relations and Trade
    
    The Shelf's fire-for-crystal dependency with Aurora Stack has produced several near-fatal crises. After the Abys∴uina devastated the subterranean city ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, surface colonies severed crystal shipments fearing the entire Berg would split; the Shelf starved in the resulting darkness. Following the Profun∴lapsum, the Shelf traded three years of crystal-debt to Aurora Stack for food under the Pactum∴ne trade charter — charity rations distributed to the youngest miners while the colony carved names into stone by the last of the fire.
    
    Fire-core shipments to surface colonies such as Promenade Hei have fallen short of Long-dark Edict requirements. Shelf couriers cite pre-Darkening supply baselines; receiving colonies reference post-Darkening adjusted baselines. The discrepancy compounds with each amendment.
    
    Under the Flipper Accord's mutual defense provisions, the Shelf dispatched Midnight Claws and Shadow Covens Order practitioners to defend Aurora Stack during the Shattered-Spire Assault. Fire-cores served as catalytic material in the casting of Grulkzul Omega Strike, an unauthorized fusion of Nightshelf fire-knowledge and orca blood-working that ended the assault, killed all casters, and further depleted reserves both colonies required.
    
    ### The Orca Compact
    
    The Foedus∴vincu was invoked to grant orca raiders diplomatic passage through the deep tunnels in exchange for surface fleet protection — sealed by the Directrix Mirror, an artifact of authentication. The Shadow Parliament refused to acknowledge the pact as authorized. After the Calving at Aurora Stack, Nightshelf miners sealed three of the tunnels the orcas had been using; the Midnight Claws refused to vacate the others. In certain passages, ice retains impressions from orca ritual-magic — fortifications broken in patterns inconsistent with conventional shore-breaker assault, fracture-lines still carrying a faint resonant frequency attributed to the Threk Boneday binding.
    
    ## Sealed Depths
    
    The **Drowned Ledge** was closed after miners breached something the Midnight Claws could not contain. Official records attribute the sealing to geological accident, but those records were maintained by Communion sympathizers whose judgment had been compromised by prolonged contact with the breach. Someone still leaves offerings at the upper locks. The outpost's intact fire-core reserves represent a strategic asset no one has reclaimed.
    
    The Shelf's deep-shrines once housed the Twilight-bells and the Thrumed~ Shadow-glass before successive thefts removed them from Nightshelf custody. The theft of the Shadow-glass by orcas Ruibung and Grandfather Blood from the Drowned Ledge itself was tried before Luminary Xuzhong Pelm'Oath; the verdict — trespass and theft but not coordinated raid activity — satisfied no one.
    
    In the deepest passages stand doors of primordial ice fused with first stone, sealed with pressure older than the aurora, marked with symbols in ash or blood by hands no living species claims. Knocking has been reported behind them in structured sequences matching no mining code. Creation scripture records that Nyla sealed them with molten core-slag and her burned flippers, warning that what creation could not kill, creation must at least contain.
    
    ## Present Condition
    
    The Shadow Parliament has not sat in full quorum for two cycles. The Midnight Claws are dissolved. The Fire Keepers hold posts they were not trained for. Aurora-crystal reserves powering the bioluminescent corridor system were classified as a finite tactical resource during the Long Dark, with consumption rates redacted from intelligence reports before first copy. Deep-vein collapse continues in the lower tunnels. Every fire-core spent on non-essential operations is subtracted from the colony's heating supply.
    
    In collapsed trading galleries, the Icebound Exchange's crude expansion tunnels intersect older Shadow Coven architecture, the two building traditions meeting in uneasy adjacency beneath sagging ceilings. The juxtaposition is instructive. Every era builds atop the last and calls it progress.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
